      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi API owners. This came up around https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/886#issuecomment-1953174126, where the WHATWG discussion had come to consensus in the 6 months since the TAG review was filed, and that discussion already covered the concerns the TAG raised. There were some improvements our team could have made to their explainer to prevent the TAG\u0027s concerns, which this change doesn\u0027t intend to cover.\n\nThis change is about how and when to tell the TAG that a design is frozen, and so it\u0027s not worth their time to review it any more. I\u0027m not sure Noam\u0027s change or my suggestions convey that exactly right, and I\u0027d love to hear more opinions.",
      "revId": "0d78fe25862e541f2fefe58ff1ec5d19b81197d0",
